  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes 15 minutes to prepare and 30 minutes to cook. It is one of the most adaptable dishes in Moroccan cooking, with the seven vegetables traditionally varying by season and household."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: The key to fluffy "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "couscous-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "couscous"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is to use boiling stock or salted water, cover tightly and leave undisturbed for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork, not a spoon, to keep the grains separate."
          }
        ]
      },
