      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 2 tbsp olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion wedges and cook for 5 minutes until starting to soften. Add the ras el hanout and black pepper and stir for 1 minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the carrot chunks and 600ml of water or vegetable stock. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat, cover and simmer for 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the courgette, red pepper and tomatoes to the pot. Replace the lid and cook for a further 10 minutes until all the vegetables are tender."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the drained chickpeas and cook for 5 minutes more to heat through. Taste and adjust the seasoning."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Meanwhile, place the couscous in a large heatproof bowl. Pour over 360ml of boiling salted water, drizzle with the remaining 2 tbsp olive oil, cover tightly with a plate or cling film and leave for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fluff the couscous with a fork. Squeeze over the lemon juice and stir through most of the herbs. Pile the couscous onto a large serving platter, spoon the vegetables and broth over the top and scatter with the remaining herbs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The couscous is clumpy"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Clumping usually means the couscous did not have enough fat or was stirred too soon. Break up any lumps by rubbing the grains between your palms after fluffing with a fork. A little extra olive oil worked in also helps."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The vegetables are mushy"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cut the vegetables into larger pieces and add them in stages, starting with the firmer carrots. Courgette and tomato need much less time than carrot and should only go in for the final 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "question": "The broth is watery and tasteless"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use vegetable stock rather than plain water, and make sure the ras el hanout is fresh and fragrant. If the broth still needs more body, simmer uncovered for 5 minutes to concentrate the flavour before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Couscous is the national dish of Morocco and a staple across North Africa. It is made from steamed semolina. The vegetables change by season and by cook. This version uses seven, which is considered lucky. Smen is a fermented Moroccan butter; you can skip it. Harissa paste stirred in before serving adds heat."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
